$\begin{align}
0.6^2 &= 0.6 \cdot 0.6
\\\\
&=0.36
\end{align}$

Since $0.6$ is six tenths, we can use fractions instead:

$\begin{align}
0.6^2 &= \dfrac{6}{10} \cdot \dfrac{6}{10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{6 \cdot 6}{10 \cdot 10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{36}{100}
\\\\
&=0.36 &&\gray{\text{(Thirty-six hundredths)}}
\end{align}$
